#: ../../topics/domains.rst:219
msgid "Cross-referencing conventions"
msgstr "Convenciones de referencias cruzadas"

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:222
msgid "Cross-references in domains support several helpful modifiers:"
msgstr "Las referencias de dominio admiten estos modificadores:"

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:224
msgid ""
"**Hide prefix**: Prefixing the target with a tilde (``~``) displays only "
"the final component of the target name. For example, "
"``:py:func:`~pipeline.reader.DocumentReader.parse``` renders as "
"``parse()``."
msgstr ""
"**Ocultar el prefijo**: anteponer ``~`` muestra solo el último "
"componente. ``:py:func:`~pipeline.reader.DocumentReader.parse``` se "
"muestra como ``parse()``."

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:225
msgid ""
"**Current scope resolution**: Relative references look up names within "
"the active module or namespace before falling back to global lookup."
msgstr ""
"**Ámbito actual**: una referencia relativa busca primero en el módulo o "
"espacio de nombres activo y luego globalmente."

#: ../../topics/domains.rst:226
msgid ""
"**Exact match**: Prefixing with a dot (``.``) searches from the current "
"module or enclosing object."
msgstr ""
"**Coincidencia exacta**: anteponer ``.`` busca desde el módulo actual o "
"el objeto contenedor."

#: ../../topics/index.rst:1
msgid "Topic guides"
msgstr "Guías temáticas"

#: ../../topics/index.rst:4
msgid ""
"These chapters explain the model. They give you enough context to make a "
"choice."
msgstr ""
"Estos capítulos explican el modelo y aportan el contexto necesario para "
"elegir."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:1
msgid "Mathematics and proofs"
msgstr "Matemáticas y demostraciones"

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:4
msgid ""
"An equation is useful when it makes a relation easier to inspect. Define "
"every symbol before relying on it. State the units where they matter. The "
"equation should support the explanation, not replace it."
msgstr ""
"Una ecuación sirve si facilita examinar una relación. Define los símbolos "
"antes de usarlos e indica las unidades pertinentes. Debe apoyar la "
"explicación, no reemplazarla."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:8
msgid "Inline and display mathematics"
msgstr "Matemáticas en línea y en bloque"

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:11
msgid ""
"Use the ``math`` role for a short expression. Use the ``math`` directive "
"for a display. Write the common LaTeX mathematics subset that both "
"targets understand."
msgstr ""
"Usa el rol ``math`` para expresiones breves y la directiva ``math`` para "
"ecuaciones independientes. Escribe el subconjunto LaTeX común a ambos "
"formatos."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:25
msgid "A side of length :math:`s` encloses area :math:`s^2`."
msgstr "Un cuadrado de lado :math:`s` tiene área :math:`s^2`\\ ."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:27
msgid "A = s^2"
msgstr "A = s^2"

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:32
msgid ""
"The relation is :eq:`area-square`. Guidedog gives a labelled equation a "
"stable target. The HTML builder supplies MathJax markup. The PDF renderer "
"translates the supported LaTeX subset to Typst mathematics. An "
"unsupported PDF command is reported. Arbitrary LaTeX packages are not "
"evaluated."
msgstr ""
"La relación es :eq:`area-square`\\ . Guidedog asigna un destino estable a "
"ecuaciones etiquetadas. HTML genera marcado MathJax; PDF convierte el "
"subconjunto LaTeX compatible a Typst. Informa de comandos PDF no "
"admitidos y no evalúa paquetes LaTeX arbitrarios."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:38
msgid "A small proof"
msgstr "Una demostración breve"

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:41
msgid ""
"Let :math:`U` be the bytes already charged to a budget. Let :math:`B` be "
"its limit. Let :math:`n` be a requested allocation. Assume all three "
"values are nonnegative and :math:`U \\le B`."
msgstr ""
"Sean :math:`U` los bytes cargados, :math:`B` el límite y :math:`n` la "
"asignación solicitada. Suponemos valores no negativos y :math:`U \\le "
"B`\\ ."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:45
msgid "**Admission rule.** Admit the request exactly when"
msgstr "**Regla de admisión.** Aceptar la solicitud si y solo si"

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:47
msgid "n \\le B - U."
msgstr "n \\le B - U."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:52
msgid "**Claim.** An admitted request preserves :math:`U + n \\le B`."
msgstr ""
"**Afirmación.** Una solicitud admitida mantiene :math:`U + n \\le B`\\ ."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:54
msgid ""
"**Proof.** Add :math:`U` to both sides of :eq:`budget-admission`. The "
"result is :math:`U+n \\le B`. The implementation tests the subtraction "
"form. It does not first compute :math:`U+n`, which could overflow a "
"machine integer. The proof and the arithmetic order agree."
msgstr ""
"**Demostración.** Suma :math:`U` a ambos lados de "
":eq:`budget-admission`\\ : resulta :math:`U+n \\le B`\\ . La "
"implementación comprueba la resta, sin calcular primero :math:`U+n`\\ , "
"que podría desbordar el entero. Prueba y orden aritmético coinciden."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:59
msgid ""
"**Boundary.** This accounts for charged host storage. It does not bound "
"the separate Typst compiler's internal allocations. A proof is only as "
"strong as the boundary it states."
msgstr ""
"**Límite.** Esto contabiliza almacenamiento del anfitrión, no las "
"asignaciones internas del compilador Typst separado. Una demostración "
"solo vale dentro del límite declarado."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:63
msgid "HTML setup"
msgstr "Configuración de HTML"

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:66
msgid ""
"These projects bundle MathJax 3.2.2 with its SVG font data. The bundle is "
"loaded only on pages containing mathematics. It makes these pages "
"readable offline after a build. No diagram script or web font service is "
"required."
msgstr ""
"Estos proyectos incluyen MathJax 3.2.2 y sus fuentes SVG, cargados solo "
"en páginas con matemáticas. Tras construir se leen sin conexión. No "
"requieren scripts de diagramas ni servicios de fuentes."

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:71
msgid ""
"For your own project, the default uses MathJax from a CDN. To serve a "
"local copy, place it in ``_static`` and set:"
msgstr ""
"En otros proyectos, MathJax se carga de un CDN por defecto. Para servir "
"una copia local, colócala en ``_static`` y configura:"

#: ../../topics/mathematics.rst:79
msgid ""
"JavaScript is needed here to typeset web equations. Without it, their "
"source remains visible. PDF equations do not need browser JavaScript. See "
"the `MathJax component contract "
"<https://docs.mathjax.org/en/v3.2/web/components/combined.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"JavaScript compone las ecuaciones web; sin él queda visible la fuente. El "
"PDF no necesita JavaScript del navegador. Consulta el `contrato de "
"componentes MathJax "
"<https://docs.mathjax.org/en/v3.2/web/components/combined.html>`_\\ ."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:1
msgid "How a project works"
msgstr "Cómo funciona un proyecto"

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:4
msgid ""
"The project root is the directory containing ``conf.toml``. ``root_doc`` "
"names the document that starts the reading order. Guidedog discovers "
"source documents, reads them, resolves their relations, and publishes a "
"complete output generation."
msgstr ""
"La raíz es el directorio de ``conf.toml``\\ . ``root_doc`` inicia el "
"orden de lectura. Guidedog descubre documentos, los lee, resuelve "
"relaciones y publica una generación completa."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:11
msgid ""
"Pipeline traverses discovery, source plugins, parallel reading, reference "
"resolution, rendering, HTML plugins, and atomic staging."
msgstr ""
"El flujo pasa por descubrimiento, plugins de fuente, lectura paralela, "
"referencias, renderizado, hooks HTML y preparación de la salida antes del "
"commit."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:11
msgid "Guidedog's end-to-end documentation compilation pipeline."
msgstr "Flujo completo de generación de documentación."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:35
msgid "Documents and resources"
msgstr "Documentos y recursos"

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:38
msgid ""
"A source suffix selects a reader. RST and project Markdown share the "
"project graph. Images and downloads are resources. Guidedog copies "
"resources that the documents use. Theme assets are listed in "
"``html_static_path``. An include must remain within the source directory "
"or the configured ``include_roots``."
msgstr ""
"El sufijo elige el lector. RST y Markdown del proyecto comparten grafo. "
"Las imágenes y descargas son recursos; se copian los utilizados. Los "
"recursos del tema van en ``html_static_path``\\ . Las inclusiones deben "
"permanecer en las fuentes o ``include_roots``\\ ."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:43
msgid "Separate projects"
msgstr "Proyectos separados"

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:46
msgid ""
"Keep a manual and design records in separate projects. They have "
"different readers and different reading orders. Each project has its own "
"configuration, templates, cache, and output. The Guidedog repository uses "
"``docs/manual`` and ``docs/gds`` this way."
msgstr ""
"Separa manual y diseños: tienen lectores y órdenes distintos. Cada "
"proyecto mantiene configuración, plantillas, caché y salida. Así se usan "
"``docs/manual`` y ``docs/gds`` en Guidedog."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:51
msgid "Incremental work"
msgstr "Compilación incremental"

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:54
msgid ""
"Guidedog records the inputs and lookups used by each output. A changed "
"source is reread. A changed dependency invalidates its users. A changed "
"template can affect every page. An unchanged document may be loaded from "
"its saved object."
msgstr ""
"Guidedog registra entradas y consultas de cada salida. Relee fuentes "
"cambiadas, invalida usuarios de dependencias modificadas y puede afectar "
"todas las páginas al cambiar plantillas. Los documentos intactos pueden "
"cargarse del objeto guardado."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:59
msgid ""
"The cache is evidence about a previous build. It is not the source of "
"truth. ``-E`` discards the saved environment for the next build. ``-a`` "
"writes all outputs. They solve different problems."
msgstr ""
"La caché es evidencia del build anterior, no la fuente de verdad. ``-E`` "
"descarta el entorno guardado para el siguiente build; ``-a`` escribe "
"todas las salidas. Resuelven problemas distintos."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:63
msgid ""
"\\text{reuse} = \\text{same inputs} \\land \\text{same lookups} \\land "
"\\text{output exists}"
msgstr ""
"\\text{reutilización} = \\text{mismas entradas} \\land \\text{mismas "
"consultas} \\land \\text{salida existente}"

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:67
msgid ""
"An explicit timestamp in a template is also an input to the rendered "
"page. A page that prints the current minute can change even when its "
"prose does not. Use ``SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`` when you need a fixed build "
"time."
msgstr ""
"Una marca temporal de plantilla también es entrada. Un minuto actual "
"puede cambiar la página sin cambiar la prosa. Usa ``SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`` "
"para fijar la hora de construcción."

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:71
msgid "Publication"
msgstr "Publicación"

#: ../../topics/projects.rst:74
msgid ""
"A build writes changes to a sibling staging directory. It completes that "
"directory, flushes the files and records, and then switches generations. "
"Readers see a complete previous or new publication. An interrupted commit "
"is settled on the next build. The design and its proof obligations are in "
":doc:`../internals/publication`."
msgstr ""
"La construcción escribe en un directorio temporal vecino. Lo completa, "
"persiste archivos y registros y cambia generaciones. El lector ve la "
"anterior o la nueva completas. La siguiente construcción resuelve commits "
"interrumpidos. Diseño y obligaciones de prueba están en "
":doc:`../internals/publication`\\ ."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:1
msgid "Typography for reading"
msgstr "Tipografía para la lectura"

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:4
msgid ""
"A page should make its structure visible before the reader studies it. A "
"strong title, a quiet navigation column, and a measured text column do "
"most of the work. Color should mark a relation or an action. It should "
"not carry the meaning alone."
msgstr ""
"La estructura debe verse antes de estudiar la página. Un título firme, "
"navegación discreta y una columna medida hacen casi todo. El color debe "
"marcar relaciones o acciones, sin llevar solo el significado."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:8
msgid "The web page"
msgstr "La página web"

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:11
msgid ""
"The custom layout has three regions: project navigation, the document, "
"and the current page's outline. Small screens use a navigation drawer. "
"The reading edition bundles Libertinus Serif and Libertinus Sans. Titles "
"use a bold serif face. Navigation, labels, and controls use its sans "
"companion. The compressed WOFF2 files are served with the site. There are "
"no font-service requests."
msgstr ""
"El diseño tiene navegación del proyecto, documento y esquema de página; "
"en pantallas pequeñas usa un panel desplegable. Incluye Libertinus Serif "
"y Sans: títulos en serif negrita y controles, etiquetas y navegación en "
"sans. Los WOFF2 comprimidos se sirven con el sitio, sin servicios "
"externos."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:20
msgid ""
"Navigation column on left, main document text column in center, local "
"section outline on right."
msgstr ""
"Navegación a la izquierda, texto en el centro y esquema de la página a la "
"derecha."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:20
msgid "Three-region reading layout for HTML documentation."
msgstr "Tres regiones de lectura en HTML."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:37
msgid ""
"**Light is the default.** The theme control also offers dark and system "
"modes. It remembers the choice on the same browser origin. System mode "
"follows the operating system. Printed HTML uses light colors. Content and "
"navigation remain usable without JavaScript. The theme control and "
"enhanced search are progressive enhancements."
msgstr ""
"**Claro es el predeterminado.** También hay oscuro y sistema, con "
"elección recordada en el mismo origen. Sistema sigue al sistema "
"operativo. El HTML impreso usa colores claros. Contenido y navegación "
"funcionan sin JavaScript; tema y búsqueda avanzada son mejoras "
"progresivas."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:43
msgid ""
"English prose can use paragraph-wide **Knuth-Plass line breaking** in the "
"browser. A small template script measures the loaded font, builds boxes, "
"spaces, and hyphenation penalties, and chooses breaks for the whole "
"paragraph. Frank Liang's pattern method supplies English hyphenation "
"candidates. The original TeX patterns and the libraries' licenses are "
"bundled with the site."
msgstr ""
"La prosa inglesa puede usar **saltos Knuth-Plass** por párrafos en el "
"navegador. Un script mide la fuente, construye cajas, espacios y "
"penalizaciones y elige los saltos del párrafo completo. El método de "
"patrones de Frank Liang propone divisiones silábicas. El sitio incluye "
"los patrones TeX originales y las licencias."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:49
msgid ""
"The enhancement preserves emphasis and the exact source text. It "
"recalculates when the reading measure changes. Copying within one "
"optimized paragraph gives the source text, without visual line divisions "
"or added hyphens. Printing restores the ordinary paragraph so the print "
"layout can paginate it."
msgstr ""
"La mejora conserva énfasis y texto exacto, recalculando al cambiar el "
"ancho. Copiar dentro de un párrafo optimizado devuelve la fuente, sin "
"divisiones visuales ni guiones añadidos. Al imprimir restaura el párrafo "
"normal para paginarlo."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:54
msgid ""
"Links, mathematics, code, interactive content, narrow measures, and other "
"languages use native browser layout. So do paragraphs for which no "
"suitably spaced solution exists. The site remains readable with "
"JavaScript disabled. The fallback uses language-aware ``hyphens: auto`` "
"and ``text-wrap: pretty``; those CSS properties alone are not a promise "
"of Knuth-Plass optimization."
msgstr ""
"Los enlaces, fórmulas, código, elementos interactivos, columnas "
"estrechas, otros idiomas y párrafos sin una solución adecuada usan la "
"composición nativa del navegador. Se puede leer sin JavaScript. "
"``hyphens: auto`` y ``text-wrap: pretty`` son la alternativa, no una "
"garantía de Knuth-Plass."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:60
msgid "The PDF page"
msgstr "La página PDF"

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:63
msgid ""
"The book template uses the same Libertinus family as the web edition. It "
"sets justified paragraphs, optimized line breaking, and language-aware "
"hyphenation. It also controls spacing, running heads, captions, code "
"blocks, and table rules. The font, hyphenation cost, and paragraph "
"measure work together. A forced line break is rarely the right repair for "
"a loose paragraph."
msgstr ""
"El libro usa Libertinus, como la web, con justificación, cortes "
"optimizados y guionado por idioma. Controla espacios, encabezados, "
"leyendas, código y tablas. Fuente, coste de guionado y ancho actúan "
"juntos. Forzar un salto rara vez arregla bien un párrafo flojo."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:69
msgid ""
"Typst optimizes the PDF paragraphs. The web enhancement optimizes "
"eligible prose. They share the source, fonts, and visual hierarchy. Their "
"line breaks can differ. See the `Typst text contract "
"<https://typst.app/docs/reference/text/text/>`_ and the `browser "
"hyphenation contract "
"<https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/hyphens>`_."
msgstr ""
"Typst optimiza los párrafos PDF; la mejora web, la prosa apta. Comparten "
"fuente, tipografías y jerarquía, pero pueden cortar distinto. Consulta el "
"`contrato de texto Typst <https://typst.app/docs/reference/text/text/>`_ "
"y el `contrato de guionado del navegador "
"<https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/hyphens>`_\\ "
"."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:74
msgid "Change the design"
msgstr "Cambiar el diseño"

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:77
msgid ""
"Edit ``_static/editorial.css`` for the documentation project's visual "
"tokens. Edit ``_templates/layout.html`` for structure. Edit "
"``_templates/book.typ`` for the print layout. Keep reading order, focus "
"indicators, labels, and sufficient contrast intact."
msgstr ""
"Edita ``_static/editorial.css`` para los tokens visuales, "
"``_templates/layout.html`` para estructura y ``_templates/book.typ`` para "
"impresión. Conserva orden de lectura, foco visible, etiquetas y contraste "
"suficiente."

#: ../../topics/typography.rst:82
msgid ""
"Build both targets after a change. Inspect a page with code, a table, a "
"diagram, and an equation. An attractive cover is not proof that the rest "
"of the book works. Build your own design in "
":doc:`../tutorial/a-custom-theme`. The full template contract is in "
":doc:`../templates`. The complete API is in :doc:`../api/index` and in "
"the same PDF book."
msgstr ""
"Después de cambiar el diseño, construya ambos formatos y revise código, "
"tablas, diagramas y fórmulas. Una buena portada no demuestra la calidad "
"del libro. Cree su tema con :doc:`../tutorial/a-custom-theme` y consulte "
":doc:`../templates`. La API completa aparece en :doc:`../api/index` y en "
"el mismo PDF."

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:1
msgid "Authoring documents"
msgstr "Redactar documentos"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:4
msgid ""
"Guidedog supports both reStructuredText (``.rst``) and MyST Markdown "
"(``.md``). Documents are parsed into a shared semantic document tree, "
"which is then used to generate both HTML websites and PDF books."
msgstr ""
"Guidedog admite reStructuredText (``.rst``) y MyST Markdown (``.md``). "
"Ambos se analizan en un árbol semántico común que genera HTML y PDF."

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:8
msgid "Choose a source language"
msgstr "Elegir el lenguaje de origen"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:11
msgid ""
"Use reStructuredText when you need full access to domains, complex "
"tables, and extensible directives. Use MyST Markdown when you prefer "
"Markdown syntax while retaining Sphinx-style directives and roles."
msgstr ""
"Use reStructuredText para dominios, tablas complejas y directivas "
"extensibles. Elija MyST Markdown si prefiere Markdown sin renunciar a "
"directivas y roles al estilo de Sphinx."

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:15
msgid ""
"In a documentation project, Markdown documents are parsed using the MyST "
"dialect. Single-document conversions with ``guidedog convert`` use "
"standard CommonMark by default, unless the MyST reader is explicitly "
"selected."
msgstr ""
"En un proyecto, Markdown se interpreta como MyST. ``guidedog convert`` "
"usa CommonMark por defecto, salvo que se seleccione MyST expresamente."

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:19
msgid "Headings and structure"
msgstr "Títulos y estructura"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:22
msgid ""
"A document title identifies the page. Sections and subsections divide the "
"text logically. In reStructuredText, headings use underline adornments "
"(and optional matching overlines). The underline must be at least as long "
"as the text."
msgstr ""
"El título identifica la página; las secciones organizan el texto. En RST "
"se subraya el título y puede añadirse una línea igual encima. La línea no "
"debe ser más corta que el título."

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:26
msgid "Recommended adornment styles:"
msgstr "Marcas de título recomendadas:"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:45
msgid ""
"Keep heading levels consistent across your project. In MyST Markdown, use "
"standard hashes (``#``, ``##``, ``###``)."
msgstr ""
"Mantenga los niveles de título coherentes. En MyST Markdown use ``#``, "
"``##`` y ``###``."

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:48
msgid "Text formatting and inline markup"
msgstr "Formato e indicaciones en línea"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:51
msgid "Use inline markup to communicate meaning rather than decoration:"
msgstr ""
"Use las marcas en línea para comunicar significado, no solo para decorar:"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:53
msgid "Inline markup"
msgstr "Marcas en línea"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:57
msgid "Style"
msgstr "Estilo"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:58
msgid "reStructuredText"
msgstr "reStructuredText"

#: ../../topics/writing.rst:59
